From 90ab57bf4f0c17a2afa1333505cab573dff60629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:45:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] test: add BIP-360 P2MR script_tests vectors and their
 generator

Adds the unit test side of Pay-to-Merkle-Root (BIP-360 v0.12.1, bitcoin/bips
commit 620871a7a442e276a058b487cd8743775fb499a4), ahead of the consensus
implementation.

test_framework/p2mr.py builds P2MR script trees, control blocks, scriptPubKeys
and bech32m v2 addresses. The tree hashing is BIP-341's, so it mirrors
taproot_tree_helper(); P2MR has no internal key and no tweak, and its control
block is 1 + 32*m bytes with the low bit of c[0] set. data/p2mr_construction.json
is the upstream construction vector file, used by feature_p2mr.py to check the
helpers against all nine official vectors before a node is started.

test/util/generate_p2mr_script_tests.py emits the P2MR rows of
src/test/data/script_tests.json, and rewrites them in place with --inplace. It
rebuilds the transaction pair that script_json_test derives from each row, so
the Schnorr signatures in those rows are real and deterministic.

Two changes to script_tests.cpp make that possible:

  - DoTest() now hands the signature checker a PrecomputedTransactionData.
    Without one CheckSchnorrSignature() reaches MissingDataBehavior::ASSERT_FAIL
    and aborts, so no row could check a real Schnorr signature. Two taproot rows
    are included to pin this down under rules that already exist.
  - The script error name table gains the taproot era errors it was missing,
    including SCHNORR_SIG and TAPROOT_WRONG_CONTROL_SIZE.

The rows that set the P2MR flag need SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR registered in
ScriptFlagNamesToEnum(); until then ParseScriptFlags() reports it as unknown.
